Let $ABC$ be a triangle with incenter $I$, circumcenter $O$, and orthocenter $H$. Let $D$, $E$, and $F$ be the feet of the perpendiculars from $A$, $B$, and $C$ to the opposite sides, respectively. Suppose $AI = 2$, $BI = 3$, $CI = 4$, and the circumradius $R = 5$. Find the perimeter of triangle $DEF$.

```asy
unitsize(0.8 cm);

pair A, B, C, D, E, F, O, I, H;

A = (0,0);
B = (4,0);
C = intersectionpoint(arc(A,5,0,180),arc(B,5,0,180));
O = (2,2*sqrt(3));
I = incenter(A,B,C);
H = extension(A,rotate(90)*(B-C),B,rotate(90)*(C-A));
D = foot(A,B,C);
E = foot(B,C,A);
F = foot(C,A,B);

draw(A--B--C--cycle);
draw(incircle(A,B,C));
draw(circumcircle(A,B,C));
draw(A--D);
draw(B--E);
draw(C--F);
draw(H--I);

label("$A$", A, SW);
label("$B$", B, SE);
label("$C$", C, N);
label("$D$", D, S);
label("$E$", E, NW);
label("$F$", F, NE);
label("$O$", O, NE);
label("$I$", I, S);
label("$H$", H, SW);
```

